<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1366].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1366&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;GBS SALTS MEDIUM FOR HYDROGENOBACTER</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaCl  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;3.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> KCl  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.15 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.3 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> MgSO<sub>4</sub>&#183;7H<sub>2</sub>O  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.123 &nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> CaCl<sub>2</sub>&#183;2H<sub>2</sub>O  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;14.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NH<sub>4</sub>Cl  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.107 &nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Mineral solution A (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1353">1353</a>)  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L   </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly and distribute the medium into culture vessels (e.g., 5.0 ml in 25 ml serum bottles/Balch tubes) under a stream of N<sub>2</sub>, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  After cooling, aseptically add per liter the following solutions (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized and stored anaerobically):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution*  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;12.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 1.0 M Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> solution  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml   </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 0.5 M Na<sub>2</sub>HPO<sub>4</sub> solution (pH 8.0)  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;20.0 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml   </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
After inoculation, add air to the gas phase (30-40% by volume) and pressurize to 100 KPa with H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (4:1, v/v) gas mixture.       <br>
